Hi,
Thank you for an incredible book and great resource. I've been using your book to plot MCC trees inferred with BEAST. I'm hoping to plot 95% CIs for node time in years. I'm a bit confused about the correct range to use for the node uncertainty. Would you be able to point me towards information about the height vs. length parameters?

Currently, I plot with:
```
ggtree(b, mrsd = mrsd)  +
  geom_range(range='height_0.95_HPD', color='grey', alpha=.6, size=2,  branch.length="height") +
  theme_tree2()
```
Thank you in advance!

On Wednesday, May 16, 2018 at 2:26:58 PM UTC-7, taua...@gmail.com wrote:
> Dear Guangchuang Yu,
>
> I am plotting a calibrated tree several hundred million years old, and using geom_range to plot the height intervals. I had not realized until now, but the bars are actually not in the right place! They have the correct length, but are slightly displaced to the right on the x axis (exactly like in this post: https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/151 <https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FGuangchuangYu%2Fggtree%2Fissues%2F151&sa=D&sntz=1&usg=AFQjCNGUmznXUbyZqIIKKXacyzF1PvnybQ>).
>
> However, I am already using > R 3.4 and ggtree 1.9.2, so maybe it is not a version issue?
>
> Do you have any idea of how to solve that? It is hard for me to send the tree as an example because it is a huge script to get to where it is now, but the case is exactly the same as in the GitHub.
>
> Please let me know what you think.
> Thank you in advance,
> Tauana

