Hi! I am having issue combining ggtree with gheatmap using facet_plot. I have tried to use the examples in the supp files from https://academic.oup.com/mbe/article/35/12/3041/5142656. But some of the examples aren't working - so its hard for me to figure out what I'm doing wrong.

Basically I have a dataframe:

library(data.table)
library(tidyverse)
library(splitstackshape)
library(ggtree)
library(ggplot2)

ID <- c("A1","A2","A3","A4","A5","A6","A7","A8","A9")
Boat  <- c("Green, Blue", "Green", "Blue","Pink, Blue, Green","Blue","Blue, Green","","Pink","Green")
Car <- c("White","White","","","White","","","","White")
Train <-c("Grey","","Grey","Grey","","Grey","Grey","","")
df <-data.frame(ID,Boat,Car,Train)

Which I then mutate to create a heatmap

df_forggplot<-df %>%
  pivot_longer(cols = -ID, names_to = "Vehicle",  values_to = "Color") %>%
  mutate(Color = str_split(Color, ",")) %>%
  unnest_longer(Color) %>%
  filter(Color != "")

And this is the outcome using _**ggplot2**_

ggplot(df, aes(x=Color, y=ID))+ #, alpha = Count)) +
  geom_tile(aes(fill=Vehicle),colour="white",size=0.5)+#, alpha = 1)
  coord_equal()

I combine dthis heatmap to my alignment using _**gheatmap**_

This is the alignment (Dummy.aln.treefile)

(A1:0.0001589189,((A2:0.0002661836,(((A3:0.0001297835,(A4:0.0016845387,Reference:0.0025983867)100/100:0.0036034778)98.8/96:0.0003588463,A5:0.0004284381)100/79:0.0000868277,A6:0.0002990092)80.7/63:0.0000472130)100/79:0.0000605054,(A7:0.0000383870,A8:0.0000304224)100/100:0.0000228026)100/79:0.0000411939,A9:0.0003248948);

And used the following to create the tree using _**ggtree**_

file_for_ggtree <- read.tree("~/Dummy.aln.treefile")
midpoint_tree<-midpoint.root(file_for_ggtree)
p<-ggtree(midpoint_tree)
p1 <- p + geom_tiplab(size=3, color="purple")

I then mutate my dataframe to suit gheatmap

df_forggtree<-cSplit(melt(as.data.table(df), 1), "value", ",", "long")[, dcast(.SD, ID ~ value, value.var = "variable")]
df_forggtree<-data.frame(column_to_rownames(df_forggtree, var = "ID"),check.names = FALSE) #assign ID to rownames for compatibility for gheatmap

And this goes as an input for gheatmap -and  it works

p2<-gheatmap(p1, df_forggtree, offset=0.000002, width=2, color=NA, colnames=TRUE,colnames_angle = 90, colnames_position= "bottom", font.size = 6 ,colnames_offset_y = 0, hjust = 1)+
  scale_fill_manual(values=c("Boat"="red","Train"="blue","Car"="Green"),
                    breaks=c("Boat","Train","Car"),name="Vehicle")
p2

But I would like to add a facet, and have tried to follow the examples in the supp file by doing it this way

facet_plot(p1, panel = "Vehicles", data = df_forggplot, geom=geom_tile, mapping = aes(x=Color, fill = Vehicle))

But then I get an error saying ```Error: Discrete value supplied to continuous scale```

I am not sure what I am doing wrong, and unfortunately some of the examples in the supp file aren't reproducible. Is this a problem with my dataframe or with facet_plot or is this a feature that hasn't been added to ggtree? I hope you can help.

